# Environment Variables

Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values before running the application.

## Application

```
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Reserved; the current runtime does not consume this setting: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api
```

## Database (PostgreSQL via Prisma)

```
# In local development, this is a comparison reference only. The development
# guard uses DEVELOPMENT_DATABASE_URL after verifying that it is distinct.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/fundedexperts

# Fill only after independently verifying a separate development branch.
DEVELOPMENT_DATABASE_URL=
DEVELOPMENT_DATABASE_CONFIRMATION=
```

## Authentication (JWT)

```
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-cryptographically-random-secret-at-least-32-characters
# Reserved; the current runtime does not consume this setting: JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d
```

## Product publication approval

```
# Required before an owner can approve a product's exact saved terms.
# Use the active ADMIN trader ID for the authorized product owner.
PRODUCT_OWNER_TRADER_ID=
```

## MT5 Integration

```
# Reserved; the current runtime does not consume this setting: MT5_API_URL=
# Reserved; the current runtime does not consume this setting: MT5_API_KEY=
# Reserved; the current runtime does not consume this setting: MT5_API_SECRET=
MT5_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
```

**Required:** `MT5_ENCRYPTION_KEY` must be at least 32 characters. Used for AES-256-GCM encryption of MT5 account credentials. If not set, credential storage is rejected.

## Planned caching / shared rate limiting (not implemented)

```
# Reserved; the current runtime does not consume this setting: REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
```

## Email (Gmail SMTP)

```
# Development/test console mode is non-delivery; no email is sent.
EMAIL_MODE=console

# Production mode uses Gmail SMTP
# EMAIL_MODE=smtp

SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your-gmail-address@gmail.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=your-google-app-password
SMTP_FROM="Funded Experts <your-gmail-address@gmail.com>"
SMTP_REPLY_TO=
```

**Gmail SMTP Notes:**
- `SMTP_PASSWORD` must be a Gmail App Password, not your Google account password.
- Generate an App Password at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
- `SMTP_USER` is the Gmail address sending the emails.
- All SMTP variables are server-only and never exposed to the browser.
- Do NOT use `NEXT_PUBLIC_SMTP_*` variables — they are removed in favor of server-only `SMTP_*`.

In development, leave `EMAIL_MODE=console` to log email previews without sending.
In production, set `EMAIL_MODE=smtp` (or leave unset) and provide real Gmail SMTP credentials.
